# ─── Production hardening additions ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Internal docs / audits (never ship to production repo)
AI_AUDIT.md
INFRASTRUCTURE_UPGRADE.md
CLAUDE*.md
*_REPORT.md
*_SUMMARY.md
*_PLAN.md
*_STRATEGY.md
*_AUDIT.md

# Temporary / debug scratch docs (directories)
notes/
scratch/
temp/
drafts/

# Root-level local scratch markdown — keep on disk, never push.
# Tracked durable root docs (do NOT add these patterns for them):
#   README.md, CLAUDE.md, TECH_DEBT.md, MASTER_ENGINEERING_ROADMAP.md,
#   PAYMENT_ARCHITECTURE.md, DEAD_CODE_REPORT.md, REPOSITORY_CONFIDENCE_PROGRAM.md,
#   PRE_DEPLOY_SEO_CHECKLIST.md
# Prefer putting new personal/session notes under notes/ or scratch/, or name them
# to match one of the patterns below so they cannot be committed by accident.
/NOTES*.md
/SESSION_*.md
/CURSOR_*.md
/WIP_*.md
/TMP_*.md
/*_SCRATCH.md
/*_LOCAL.md
/*_SESSION_NOTES.md

# Local testing artifacts
manual-test*
test-output*
logs/
.voice-verify-out/
.verify-out/
*.log
failed-emails.csv
/screenshots/
/lighthouse*.json
/audit-phase1*.png
/phase1-*.png
scripts/seo-audit-report.json
scripts/gsc-audit-report.json
scripts/gsc-audit-report.md
scripts/gsc-authoritative-audit.json
scripts/gsc-authoritative-audit.md
scripts/email-runtime-validation-results.json

# Claude / AI session scratch outputs
.claude/
claude-output/
ai-output/

# OS / editor junk
Thumbs.db

# Ensure env files never commit (re-state explicitly; .env.example is safe to track)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Exceptions to the "Production hardening additions" internal-docs patterns above
# (CLAUDE*.md / *_REPORT.md / *_PLAN.md / *_STRATEGY.md) — those patterns are broad
# by design, but they were silently blocking `git add` on core engineering-program
# documents that must be trackable: CLAUDE.md (the operating manual every session
# reads first — previously untracked with no exception, meaning a fresh clone or CI
# checkout would be missing it entirely) and three planning docs from the 2026-07
# engineering program. Discovered and fixed 2026-07-05 (Task 1A.5) — if a new
# internal-only scratch doc happens to match one of these suffixes, it stays
# ignored by default; only the files named below are explicitly re-included.
!CLAUDE.md
!DEAD_CODE_REPORT.md
!docs/RELEASE_STRATEGY.md
!docs/OBSERVABILITY_EXECUTION_PLAN.md
